invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: ct.h takes the X25519=wide field beside WIDEMUL=runtime, so an object
  built outside the Makefile runs the 64x64->128 multiply its build
  stated for every session, whatever each session answers.
  test/widemul-builds.sh requires that build not to compile.

--- old
#ifdef CH_WIDEMUL_RUNTIME
#error "X25519=wide states its multiply's timing at build time; WIDEMUL=runtime asks each session"
#endif
--- new
